{"_meta":{"openai/widgetAccessible":true,"ui":{"visibility":["model","app"]}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Find Devices and Services"},"description":"Find devices/services, declarations and observations. Filter by name/type/capability; follow paginationContext.nextToken for the requested scope. endpointId reads one known endpoint and takes no query, maxResults or nextToken. Copy returned references/account; Port OS selects routes. Use group_query for rooms and management tools for inventory edits.\n\nState reads require declared expand capabilities and forceDeviceAttributeQuery=true. FRESH is current; STALE is last known with sampledAt and cannot support a safety claim. Missing/invalid/errored/PROVIDER_NO_STATE is unknown; PROVIDER_NO_STATE is not offline and retries cannot supply an absent provider value. FRESH UNREACHABLE is offline; STALE connectivity is last known. ID-only lookup reads metadata. simulator:true means all routes are synthetic; routes[].simulator marks mixed routes. Missing flags are unknown. Exclude simulated routes from household claims unless explicitly selected; their readings do not prove physical state.\n\nTypes alone do not identify lamps: switches/plugs require confirmed lighting assignment. Temperature setpoints are distinct from ambient readings; clarify indoor/outdoor ambiguity. Check relevant authorized accounts before reporting absence; names alone prove no identity. Select concrete route-backed services, not provider catalogs or obsolete unrouted entries. Default lists include ENABLED; DISABLED or * selects others. Exact endpointId can read disabled metadata. controllableGroups needs group:read. Device workflows and payloads: matching Port OS skill or portos://guides/index.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"enablement":{"default":"ENABLED","description":"Filter by ENABLED (default), DISABLED, or * for both. This filter is preserved by pagination.","enum":["ENABLED","DISABLED","*"],"type":"string"},"endpointId":{"description":"Return one endpoint by its full Port OS identifier. Cannot be combined with other filters or pagination. Results advertise its declared command and outbound message IDs.","type":"string"},"expand":{"description":"Select observations to add to each device result, for example [\"power\", \"connectivity\"] or [\"battery\"]. Use capability names or full namespaces declared by the device. This reads attributes; it does not send commands or broaden the device search. Short names use port1/systems/zero/capability-interfaces. No state reads by default.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"forceDeviceAttributeQuery":{"description":"Read selected attributes from devices instead of cache. Requires nonempty expand. Failed reads remain unavailable.","type":"boolean"},"maxResults":{"description":"Maximum number of results (default 10, maximum 100).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"nextToken":{"description":"Opaque cursor returned by a previous endpoint_query call.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"Optional field-first filter. Omit it to load full context; filter only when the account is large. Each key is a field or a combinator, and all keys of one object must match: {\"name\": {\"like\": \"living\"}, \"type\": {\"in\": [\"LIGHT\", \"SWITCH\"]}}. Combinators: {\"and\": [query, ...]}, {\"or\": [query, ...]}, {\"not\": query}. Text operators: eq (exact), in (any of a list), like (case-insensitive substring), lt and gt (lexical order). List operators: has (contains the exact value), like (some value contains the substring, case-insensitive). Fields: id (text) returned endpoint ID; name (text) endpoint name; type (text) effective endpoint type, including customer overrides, such as LIGHT, SWITCH, PLUG or ROBOT_VACUUM; manufacturer (text) manufacturer name; model (text) model name; ownerId (text, eq only at the top level) principal whose endpoints to list; defaults to the caller; interfaces (list) full capability interface namespaces; messages (list) returned message IDs the endpoint accepts; controllableGroups (list) IDs of groups the endpoint can act on, such as rooms a vacuum can clean (needs group:read).","properties":{},"type":"object"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"endpoint_query","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"ErrorCode":{"enum":["BAD_REQUEST","UNAUTHORIZED","FORBIDDEN","INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE","NOT_FOUND","CONFLICT","UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY","UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION","TOO_MANY_REQUESTS","SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE","NOT_IMPLEMENTED","INTERNAL","CHECKSUM_MISMATCH","FILE_TOO_LARGE","STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE","INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS","INVALID_FILE_TYPE","QUOTA_EXCEEDED","CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION","ENDPOINT_UNREACHABLE","BRIDGE_UNREACHABLE","CLOUD_CONTROL_DISABLED","ENDPOINT_BUSY","ENDPOINT_LOW_POWER","AUTHORIZATION_CREDENTIAL_INVALID","AUTHORIZATION_CREDENTIAL_EXPIRED","INVALID_DIRECTIVE","INVALID_VALUE","VALUE_OUT_OF_RANGE","NOT_SUPPORTED_IN_CURRENT_MODE","RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED","PROVIDER_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE","PROVIDER_TIMEOUT","PROVIDER_INTERNAL_ERROR","INVALID_PROVIDER_RESPONSE","OUTCOME_UNKNOWN","PRECONDITION_FAILED","AUTH_LINK_NOT_READY","AUTH_LINK_NOT_DISCONNECTABLE","PRECONDITION_REQUIRED","IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REQUIRED","IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED","IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_IN_FLIGHT","IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_INVALID","GROUP_MERGED","MULTI_ROOM_UNSUPPORTED","MAP_NOT_ACTIVE","TARGET_UNSUPPORTED","TARGET_AMBIGUOUS","TARGET_GROUP_NOT_FOUND","TARGET_GROUP_DISABLED","DUPLICATE_TARGET_GROUP","MESSAGE_UNSUPPORTED","MESSAGE_AMBIGUOUS","ENDPOINT_DISABLED","ENDPOINT_ROUTE_CHANGED","ENDPOINT_HAS_DEPENDENCIES","ENDPOINT_EVENT_SUBSCRIPTIONS_ACTIVE","ENDPOINT_COMMITTED_CLEANUP_PENDING","DEEP_QUERY_FAILED","PROVIDER_NO_STATE","EVENT_MANAGEMENT_DISABLED","SUBSCRIPTION_IDENTITY_IMMUTABLE","UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE","EVENT_PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE","REQUEST_BODY_TOO_LARGE","EVENT_IDENTITY_CONFLICT","EVENT_INGRESS_QUOTA_EXCEEDED","EVENT_RECEIPT_EXPIRED","EVENT_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE","EVENT_